@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-calendar`

-- ca-tests-holidays.l4
--
-- Section 26 (a time limit that expires or falls on a holiday), section 35(1) "holiday", "standard time" and "commencement", and section 29.
-- The calendars are SUPPLIED BY EACH TEST, as the module requires; the module has none of its own.
-- Weekdays below were checked with a calendar outside L4 (python3 `datetime`):
--   2026-03-07 Saturday, 2026-03-08 Sunday, 2026-03-09 Monday, 2026-03-10 Tuesday, 2026-03-11 Wednesday;
--   2026-09-06 Sunday, 2026-09-07 Monday (first Monday in September), 2026-09-30 Wednesday;
--   2028-07-16 Sunday; 2030-09-01 Sunday, 2030-09-02 Monday (first Monday in September), 2030-09-03 Tuesday.
-- Section 35(1) lists Sunday and does NOT list Saturday.

§ `Section 26 with a calendar the test supplies: Sundays only`

-- A last day that is not a holiday stays: Friday 6 March, Saturday 7 March (Saturday is not a holiday), Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 6) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 6
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 7
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- A last day that is a Sunday moves to the day next following that is not a holiday: Monday.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9

§ `Section 26 with several holidays in a row, all supplied by the test`

-- Sunday 8 March, then Monday 9 March a holiday: Tuesday 10 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
-- Sunday 8, Monday 9 and Tuesday 10 March holidays: Wednesday 11 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9 OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 11
-- A calendar the test supplies in which Saturday and Sunday are days of rest: the last day Saturday 7 March moves past both to Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is weekend` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- A holiday BEFORE the last day does not move it; and a last day that is not a holiday does not move because the day after is one.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 8 OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- Across a month end: a holiday on 31 January and on 1 February.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31 OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2
-- Across a year end.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31 OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2

§ `Section 26: the search is bounded at 366 days, a bound of this encoding and not of the Act`

-- If days 1 to 365 after the last day are holidays and day 366 is not, the answer is day 366.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST YMD 2026 1 1 AND d AT MOST (YMD 2026 1 1) PLUS 365) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 1) PLUS 366
-- If the first 366 days after it are all holidays, the answer is a refusal, not a date.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST YMD 2026 1 1 AND d AT MOST (YMD 2026 1 1) PLUS 366))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD TRUE))

§ `Section 26 on each unit: the last day of the period, then the day the thing may be done`

-- Section 26 names "the time limited for the doing of a thing" and says nothing of its unit: it applies to days, months and years alike.
-- One month after 8 February 2026: the period ends Sunday 8 March, so the thing may be done Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done within` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- One year after 8 March 2025: the period ends Sunday 8 March 2026, so Monday 9 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done within` 1 `years after` (YMD 2025 3 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- Seven days after 1 March 2026 ends Sunday 8 March: Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done within` 7 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 1) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- Thirty days after 1 January 2026 ends Saturday 31 January, which is not a holiday: it stays.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done within` 30 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- One month after 31 January 2025 ends Friday 28 February: it stays.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done within` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- The period itself is never moved: it still ends on its own last day.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8))'s `the last day`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 8

§ `Whether a thing may be done on a day within a period whose last day is a holiday`

-- Period: one month after 8 February 2026, 9 February to Sunday 8 March; the thing may be done on Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 2 9) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d)
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 6) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d)
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d)
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d))
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 2 8) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d))
-- Two holidays at the end: the period ends Sunday 8 March, Monday 9 March is also a holiday: the day named is Tuesday 10 March, and Monday 9 March is neither inside the period nor the named day.
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9))
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 8)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9))
-- A period whose last day is not a holiday has no extension: it ends Friday 6 March; Saturday 7 March is outside it.
#ASSERT `a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 6) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 6)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing may be done on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `within the time limited by` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2026 2 6)) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d))

§ `Section 26: a day of rest, a recess or a closed office that is not a holiday`

-- The only day-off word in the text is "holiday".  A caller who asks about another kind gets a refusal, not a guess.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the last day for a thing where the time limited ends on a day of rest, a recess or a closed office that is not a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 7))

§ `Section 35(1) "holiday": the days the text dates`

-- Sunday.
#ASSERT `is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 3 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 3 7))
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Sunday` (YMD 2026 3 9))
-- "the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day".
#ASSERT `is Labour Day` (YMD 2026 9 7)
#ASSERT `is Labour Day` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT `is Labour Day` (YMD 2030 9 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`is Labour Day` (YMD 2026 9 14))
#ASSERT NOT (`is Labour Day` (YMD 2025 9 8))
#ASSERT NOT (`is Labour Day` (YMD 2026 9 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`is Labour Day` (YMD 2026 8 31))
-- "National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30".
#ASSERT `is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT `is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` (YMD 2025 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` (YMD 2026 9 29))
#ASSERT NOT (`is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` (YMD 2026 10 1))
-- Together, with no other holidays supplied.
#ASSERT `is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 9 7)
#ASSERT `is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT `is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 3 8)
-- Saturday is not a holiday; neither is an ordinary Tuesday.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 3 7))
#ASSERT NOT (`is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 3 10))
-- The days the text names but does not date are the caller's: Christmas Day is a holiday only if the caller says 25 December is.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `no other holidays` (YMD 2026 12 25))
#ASSERT `is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 25) (YMD 2026 12 25)

§ `Section 26 with the Act's own dated holidays and the caller's other holidays`

-- Sunday 8 March 2026: Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
-- Saturday stays.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 7
-- Sunday 6 September 2026, then Labour Day Monday 7 September: Tuesday 8 September.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 9 6) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 8
-- 30 September 2026, a Wednesday: the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, so Thursday 1 October.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 9 30) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 1
-- Sunday 8 March 2026 and the caller's own holiday on Monday 9 March: Tuesday 10 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the other holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10

§ `The worked cases whose last day falls on a holiday`

-- Three years after 16 July 2025: the period ends Sunday 16 July 2028; the thing may be done Monday 17 July 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 17
-- Five years after 1 September 2025: the period ends Sunday 1 September 2030; Monday 2 September 2030 is Labour Day; so Tuesday 3 September 2030.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 9 1))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2030 9 3
-- The other worked cases end on a day that is not a holiday: Tuesday 15 January 2030, Saturday 31 January 2026, Saturday 28 February 2026, Friday 28 February 2025 (twice).
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 1 15))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 30 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` ((`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))'s `the last day`) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

§ `Section 35(1) "standard time" and section 29`

#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `Newfoundland standard time` EQUALS 210
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `Atlantic standard time` EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `eastern standard time` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `central standard time` EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `mountain standard time` EQUALS 420
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `Pacific standard time` EQUALS 480
#ASSERT `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` `Yukon standard time` EQUALS 540
-- Whole provinces and territories.
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Newfoundland standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Nova Scotia` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Atlantic standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of New Brunswick` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Atlantic standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Prince Edward Island` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Atlantic standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Manitoba` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `central standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Saskatchewan` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `mountain standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Alberta` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `mountain standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Northwest Territories` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `mountain standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Pacific standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `Yukon` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Yukon standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `Southampton Island or an island adjacent to Southampton Island` `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `eastern standard time`
-- Quebec: east of the 63rd meridian of west longitude is Atlantic (so a west longitude below 63), west of it is eastern.
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`the Province of Quebec` 60) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Atlantic standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`the Province of Quebec` 70) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `eastern standard time`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`the Province of Quebec` 63) `unless` NOTHING)
-- Ontario: between the 68th and the 90th meridians is eastern; west of the 90th is central; east of the 68th the text gives nothing.
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`the Province of Ontario` 80) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `eastern standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`the Province of Ontario` 95) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `central standard time`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`the Province of Ontario` 90) `unless` NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`the Province of Ontario` 68) `unless` NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`the Province of Ontario` 60) `unless` NOTHING)
-- Nunavut: east of the 68th Atlantic; 68th to 85th eastern; 85th to 102nd central; west of the 102nd mountain.
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 60) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `Atlantic standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 75) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `eastern standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 90) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `central standard time`
#ASSERT `the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 110) `unless` NOTHING EQUALS `mountain standard time`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 85) `unless` NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standard time of` (`Nunavut` 102) `unless` NOTHING)
-- "except as otherwise provided by any proclamation": the proclaimed time wins.
#ASSERT `the standard time of` `the Province of Alberta` `unless` (JUST `Pacific standard time`) EQUALS `Pacific standard time`
-- Section 29: a specified time of the day is standard time.  09:00 in British Columbia is 540 minutes after midnight there, 1020 after Greenwich midnight.
#ASSERT (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 540 `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)'s `minutes after Greenwich midnight` EQUALS 1020
#ASSERT (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 540 `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)'s `whole days after the day specified` EQUALS 0
-- 20:00 in British Columbia is 04:00 Greenwich the next day.
#ASSERT (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 1200 `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)'s `minutes after Greenwich midnight` EQUALS 240
#ASSERT (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 1200 `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)'s `whole days after the day specified` EQUALS 1
-- Midnight in Newfoundland is 03:30 Greenwich.
#ASSERT (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 0 `at` `the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador` `unless` NOTHING)'s `minutes after Greenwich midnight` EQUALS 210
-- A time that is not a minute of the day is refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` 1440 `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` (0 MINUS 1) `at` `the Province of British Columbia` `unless` NOTHING)
-- "local time" is a fact about a place that the Act does not state.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the minutes behind Greenwich time of the local time of` `the Province of British Columbia`)
